UPDATE companies SET description='Mississippi Farm Tables operates from Carthage, Mississippi. The company was founded by Mark and Helen, whose story began with Mark''s upbringing in Ireland where the kitchen table served as the family nucleus. After community work in London and a rekindled romance in France, Mark discovered woodworking under a master artisan in rural France. The couple later relocated to Mississippi to establish the business.

The workshop produces custom farmhouse dining tables, chairs, and a range of occasional tables including coffee, sofa, console, and end tables, as well as benches. Each piece is handcrafted to order, with customers selecting dimensions, shape, wood species, and finish. To date, the shop has completed nearly 500 tables.

The founders state their mission is to revive the tradition of family meals and meaningful conversation around the table. A separate initiative, Coffee Tables for Cancer, directs 10 percent of proceeds from coffee table sales to cancer research funding.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom woodworking", "Furniture manufacturing", "Custom finishing", "Design consultation", "Handcrafted assembly"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Home furnishings", "Custom furniture"], "materials": ["Wood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Fully customizable dimensions, shape, wood species, and finish", "Handcrafted by expert craftsmen", "Nearly 500 tables built to date", "Coffee Tables for Cancer donates 10% of proceeds to research"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Carthage, Mississippi -> db", "Founders Mark and Helen -> /about", "Mark''s upbringing in Ireland with kitchen table tradition -> /about", "Woodworking passion ignited in rural France under master artisan -> /about", "Relocated to Mississippi after romance in France -> /about", "Nearly 500 tables built -> /about", "Customizable options: size, shape, wood type, finish -> /", "Handcrafted farm tables -> /", "Products: coffee tables, sofa tables, console tables, end tables, benches -> /", "Mission to bring families back to the table -> /about", "Coffee Tables for Cancer donates 10% of proceeds to cancer research -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Custom Farmhouse Dining Tables & Chairs", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mississippi-farm-tables' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Mississippi Silicon operates a silicon metal production facility in Burnsville, Mississippi. The plant launched in late 2015, becoming the first new domestic silicon metal smelter built in the United States in four decades. The company is structured as a partnership between Rima Holding USA, Inc. (the majority owner, linked to Brazilian ferroalloy producer Rima Industrial S/A) and Clean Tech I LLC, a group of strategic investors and financial advisers.

The facility produces raw silicon metal using submerged electric arc furnaces that reduce quartz or gravel (SiO₂) with a carbon source to yield 99% pure molten silicon, which is tapped in batches. Mississippi Silicon invested over $200 million in the Burnsville site and now supplies roughly 10% of the silicon metal consumed in the U.S. The operation emphasizes modern furnace controls, proprietary process techniques, and automated off-gas containment to achieve low-cost, high-quality output.

The company sells silicon metal to customers that serve automotive, electronics, steel, and a broad range of consumer, industrial, and commercial markets across North America and globally. Automotive manufacturing is cited as a key end-use sector, alongside electronics and steel production.

Mississippi Silicon was established to restore domestic silicon metal supply, leveraging low-cost Tennessee Valley Authority electricity, proximity to raw-material sources in Mississippi, Alabama, and Kentucky, and advanced automation to become one of the world’s lowest-cost and highest-quality producers. The venture also aims to create jobs in northeast Mississippi.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Submerged electric arc furnace operation", "Quartz/gravel reduction with carbon reductant", "Molten silicon tapping and casting", "Batch processing with continuous furnace operation", "Advanced process automation and control", "Off-gas capture and containment", "Quality management per ISO 9001"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Electronics", "Steel", "Consumer goods", "Industrial", "Commercial"], "materials": ["Quartz (SiO2)", "Carbon reductant", "Electricity"], "equipment": ["Submerged arc furnace"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Modern submerged electric arc furnace technology", "Proprietary operating techniques developed by management and Rima", "Low-cost electricity from Tennessee Valley Authority", "Proximity to competitively priced raw materials in the tri-state region", "Advanced process automation for consistent quality"], "facts_used": ["First domestic silicon metal plant in 40 years, produces ~10% of US silicon metal -> /", "Launch in late 2015 -> /", "Partnership between Rima Holding USA, Inc. and Clean Tech I LLC -> /", "Rima Holding USA majority owner, associated with Rima Industrial S/A (Brazil) -> /", "Clean Tech I LLC composed of strategic investors and financial advisers -> /", "Invested over $200 million in Burnsville facility -> /", "Works with Mississippi, Alabama, Kentucky companies for raw materials and TVA for electricity -> /", "ISO 9001 certification from Dekra -> /", "Process: submerged arc furnace, quartz/gravel + carbon, reduction to 99% silicon, batch tapping -> /about-us", "Modern Submerged Electric Arc technology, proprietary techniques, low-cost electricity, proximity to raw materials, advanced automation -> /about-us", "One of lowest cost and highest quality producers globally -> /about-us", "Sells to customers serving automotive, electronics, steel, consumer, industrial, commercial markets -> /", "Automotive manufacturing industry highlighted -> db", "Headquarters Burnsville, Mississippi -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Mississippi Silicon is the first domestic manufacturer of raw silicon metal built in the past 40 years and produces approximately 10% of all silicon metal used in the United States.", "founded_year": "2015", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mississippi-silicon' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Mississippi Solar, LLC is based in Eupora, Mississippi. The company was founded in 2008 by Will and Carolyn Hegman and officially registered with the Mississippi Secretary of State in 2009. It was the first commercial electrical contractor in the state to receive a Specialty Wind & Solar classification. Today the business is owned and operated by John and Virginia Wilbanks, both Mississippi natives, and remains family-owned.

The firm designs and installs turn-key solar photovoltaic and battery-backup systems for residential and commercial customers across Mississippi. It also sells, installs, and services Generac home and business standby generators in more than 20 counties, and fits Level 2 and 3 EV charging stations, energy-management thermostats, and LP-tank monitoring. The company acts as a commercial electrical contractor and residential builder, handling permitting, project management, and ongoing system monitoring.

Mississippi Solar serves homeowners, businesses, farms, and institutional clients. Early projects included a poultry farm, a sports arena, and the state''s first commercial utility-scale solar PV system as well as the first grid-tie and grid-tie-with-battery installations under the TVA Generation Partners program. The company also supports generator customers in counties such as Lafayette, Pontotoc, Lee, and Lowndes.

The company emphasizes its local roots and code expertise, NABCEP-certified installers, and status as a Generac Power Pro Elite Plus dealer. It backs installations with a 25-year module warranty through REC Solar, lifetime system monitoring, and a five-year workmanship warranty. Its stated mission is to empower customers with reliable, worry-free energy independence, sustainability, and backup power.', certifications=ARRAY['NABCEP','Mississippi Specialty Wind & Solar Classification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar PV system design and installation", "Battery backup system design and installation", "Generac standby generator sales, installation, service, and maintenance", "EV charging station installation (Level 2 and Level 3)", "Energy management system installation (Ecobee, Generac Smart Thermostats)", "LP tank monitoring installation", "Electrical contracting (commercial and residential)", "Project management and permitting", "System monitoring and preventive maintenance", "Financing and incentive consultation"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Agricultural", "Utility"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["First Mississippi electrical contractor with Specialty Wind & Solar classification", "NABCEP-certified installation team", "Generac Power Pro Elite Plus dealer for sales, service, and warranty", "25-year module warranty via REC Solar partnership", "Lifetime system monitoring included with every installation"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2008 by Will and Carolyn Hegman -> /about-us", "Officially registered with Mississippi Secretary of State in 2009 -> /about-us", "First commercial contractor in Mississippi with Specialty Wind & Solar classification -> /about-us", "First commercial utility solar PV system in the state -> /about-us", "First grid-tie and grid-tie with battery backup under TVA Generation Partners program -> /about-us", "Currently owned and operated by John and Virginia Wilbanks -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Eupora, Mississippi -> /about-us", "Provides solar installation statewide -> /about-us", "Offers Generac generator sales, installation, service in 20+ counties -> /about-us", "NABCEP certified installers -> /", "Generac Power Pro Elite Plus dealer -> /", "Designs and installs turn-key solar PV and backup power solutions -> /", "Installs Level 2 and 3 EV charging stations -> /", "Installs energy management solutions (Ecobee, Generac Smart Thermostats) -> /", "LP tank monitoring -> /", "25-year module warranty via REC Solar -> /about-us", "Lifetime system monitoring -> /about-us", "Five-year workmanship warranty -> /about-us", "Family-owned and Mississippi natives -> /", "Mission: empower customers with reliable, worry-free energy independence -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Mississippi Solar, LLC is a Mississippi owned and operated Commercial Electrical Contractor and Residential Builder.", "founded_year": "2008", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mississippi-solar-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Missoula Bench Builder operates from Missoula, Montana, where founder Ryan Hollingsworth designs and builds custom furniture from reclaimed materials sourced from the state’s historic structures.

The shop produces one-of-a-kind tables, bookcases, bars, benches, and other furniture using a three-step collaborative process: clients select reclaimed materials, Hollingsworth develops a design, and the finished piece is delivered. All work is performed in-house, with each item handcrafted to the customer’s specifications.

Missoula Bench Builder differentiates itself through responsibly reclaimed materials, fully custom designs, and the “Montana Made” provenance of every piece built personally by Hollingsworth.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom Furniture", "Reclaimed Wood Furniture", "Custom Tables", "Custom Bookcases", "Custom Design Woodworking"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Reclaimed wood", "Barnwood", "Historic building materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Responsibly reclaimed materials from Montana historic buildings", "Fully custom design collaboration", "Montana-made, handcrafted by Ryan Hollingsworth", "Simple three-step client process"], "facts_used": ["Name, location, capabilities -> db", "Founder Ryan Hollingsworth, reclaimed materials from historic Montana buildings, three-step process, testimonials -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Each piece of furniture designed and brought to life by you and Missoula Bench Builder, Ryan Hollingsworth, preserves a piece of history through the reclaimed materials of Montana\u2019s most historic buildings.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='missoula-bench-builder' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Missouri Medical Supply, Inc. was established in 1996 in St. Louis, Missouri, to provide high-quality home medical equipment and services that help individuals maintain independence and quality of life at home. The company operates from its location in St. Louis.

The firm supplies a range of home medical equipment and acts as an authorized Medicare provider and a contracted provider for numerous insurance companies.

Its customer base includes hospitals, nursing homes, assisted living facilities, rehabilitation facilities, dialysis centers, and home care agencies across the region. The company focuses on the healthcare and home-healthcare sectors, providing equipment and services to both institutional and residential clients.

Missouri Medical Supply emphasizes a quick and easy Medicare claims process and offers state-of-the-art equipment for independent living. The business was founded to address the need for reliable home medical equipment and supportive services for those requiring assistance with daily living.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Medical equipment supply", "Medicare claims processing", "Insurance billing"], "industries": ["Hospitals", "Nursing homes", "Assisted living facilities", "Rehabilitation facilities", "Dialysis centers", "Home care agencies"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Authorized Medicare provider", "Contracted with multiple insurance companies", "Quick Medicare claims processing", "Serves hospitals, nursing homes, and home care agencies", "State-of-the-art home medical equipment for independent living"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1996 -> db", "Headquarters St. Louis, Missouri -> db", "Authorized Medicare provider -> /", "Contracted provider for many insurance companies -> /", "Serves hospitals, nursing homes, assisted living facilities, rehabilitation facilities, dialysis centers, home care agencies -> /", "Address 8523 Olive Blvd, Saint Louis, MO 63132 -> /", "Phone  -> /", "Hours Mon-Fri 9-5:30 CST, Sat by appointment -> /", "Website momedsupply.com -> db", "Quick and easy Medicare claims process -> /", "State-of-the-art home medical equipment for independent living -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Missouri Medical Supply, Inc. was established in 1996 to provide the highest quality equipment and services to those who need help maintaining independence and quality of life at home.", "founded_year": "1996", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='missouri-medical-supply' AN