UPDATE companies SET description='Missouri Reclaimed Furniture operates from Springfield, Missouri, where founder David began crafting custom pieces from salvaged barn wood. The company''s exact founding year is not publicly stated, but its focus on reclaiming history through wood deconstruction has defined its work since inception.

The shop produces customized cabinetry, custom furniture, and offers cabinet resurfacing, wood flooring replacement, and wood door repair. Each piece is handcrafted from reclaimed barn wood, selected for its rustic character and unique patina. No facility size or headcount figures are disclosed.

The company serves residential customers across Missouri and beyond, providing one-of-a-kind furnishings and renovation services for homeowners seeking distinctive, environmentally responsible woodwork.

David emphasizes environmental responsibility through the deconstruction and reuse of quality materials, giving each creation a story rooted in the wood''s history. The combination of traditional craftsmanship and reclaimed materials positions the business as a source for true custom work with a sustainable ethos.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cabinetry", "Cabinet resurfacing", "Custom furniture manufacturing", "Wood flooring installation", "Wood door repair", "Reclaimed wood deconstruction"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Custom cabinetry", "Home renovation"], "materials": ["Reclaimed barn wood", "Salvaged wood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Environmentally responsible deconstruction and reuse of materials", "Handcrafted unique pieces with rustic character", "True custom work from reclaimed barn wood", "Customized cabinetry, furniture, and repair services"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Springfield, Missouri -> db", "Founder: David -> /", "Services: Customized cabinetry, cabinet resurfacing, custom furniture, wood flooring replacement, wood door repair -> /", "Materials: Reclaimed barn wood, salvaged wood -> /", "Environmental focus: Deconstruction and reuse of quality materials -> /", "Company description: Furnishing homes with reclaimed barn wood -> /", "Tagline: History Salvaged. Beauty Reclaimed. True Custom Work. -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Customized cabinetry, Cabinet resurfacing, Custom furniture, Replace wood flooring, Repair wood doors", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='missouri-reclaimed-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Mobius Materials is based in Richmond, Virginia. The company was founded by Margaret Upshur, who serves as CEO. Upshur started the business after experiencing the waste of excess electronic components and high procurement costs while operations at an IoT module manufacturer; she created Mobius to fix that breakdown and return unused parts to the supply chain.

The company operates as a distributor and reseller of electronic components, specializing in verified integrated circuits (ICs) from major manufacturers such as Texas Instruments, Analog Devices, Vishay, Murata, Onsemi, Microchip, STMicroelectronics, and NXP Semiconductors. It sources certified parts, tests them for authenticity, and also purchases excess inventory from manufacturers. The platform provides a marketplace for buying and selling components, with services including bill-of-materials (BOM) optimization and contract manufacturing services. Millions of parts are listed in stock across the supported manufacturer lines.

Mobius serves electronics manufacturers, including IoT module makers and hardware manufacturers. Customers include CEOs and operations leaders at manufacturing companies who need to reduce component costs and manage excess inventory. For example, Hailey N., CEO of a manufacturer, reported saving 25% on BOM costs, and Kendell W., a Manufacturing & Operations Leader, increased excess inventory sales from fewer than two parts per month to over ten orders monthly.

The company differentiates itself by vetting suppliers and comprehensively testing part authenticity, offering 10–70% off common parts at market rates, and providing access to rare stock from other manufacturers'' excess. Its stated mission is to improve manufacturers'' P&L and get unused parts back into the supply chain.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electronic component sourcing", "Component authenticity testing", "Excess inventory purchasing", "Electronic component distribution", "Bill of materials (BOM) optimization", "Contract manufacturing services"], "industries": ["Electronics manufacturing", "IoT device manufacturing", "Hardware manufacturing"], "materials": ["Integrated circuits (ICs)", "Electronic components"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Under two weeks for certified parts sourcing", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vetted suppliers with comprehensive authenticity testing", "10\u201370% off common parts at market rates", "Access to rare stock from other manufacturers'' excess", "BOM optimization saving 25% cost", "Excess inventory sales increased from <2 to >10 orders per month"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Richmond, Virginia -> db", "Founder Margaret Upshur, CEO -> homepage", "Company started to address excess component waste -> homepage", "Sells verified ICs from major manufacturers -> homepage", "Offers authenticity testing -> homepage", "Buys excess inventory -> homepage", "Serves electronics manufacturers, IoT module makers -> homepage", "Customer testimonial from Hailey N. (CEO) and Kendell W. (Manufacturing & Operations Leader) -> homepage", "Lead time under two weeks for certified parts -> homepage", "Contract manufacturing services mentioned -> db"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We sell verified ICs from reputable manufacturers.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mobius-materials' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Modern Edge Metal Fabrication operates from a 6,000-square-foot shop in West Bath, Maine. The company traces its roots to 2015 when Luke Winne, a Georgetown native who grew up around his father’s machine shop, launched a one-man operation out of his dad’s 16-by-24-foot building after a decade honing his craft in Montana. Winne incorporated the business in 2020, and his wife Mandy joined the family-owned venture in 2021.

The shop provides full-service metal fabrication — architectural, structural, marine, and production work — using MIG, TIG, and stick welding (including portable units), a manual lathe, knee mill, 48-inch sheet metal brake (11-gauge mild steel capacity), 80-ton ironworker, 13-by-21-inch band saw, plasma cutting, and 3D modeling. A small team of craftsmen handles design, engineering, fabrication, finishing, and installation in-house.

Customers include general contractors, architects, marine contractors, shipyards, furniture designers, and agricultural operators such as wild blueberry and vegetable farms. The company has fabricated and installed over 8,000 lineal feet of cable railing in midcoast Maine and built the 18-foot Cape Elizabeth Lighthouse replica for the Maine Maritime Museum’s permanent exhibit.

Winne founded Modern Edge to turn a childhood passion for metalworking into a business built on long-term relationships and word-of-mouth referrals. The firm emphasizes a design-through-install workflow, mirror-finish stainless capabilities with in-house passivation, and a proprietary cable rail system priced competitively with national brands.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Architectural metal fabrication", "Structural fabrication", "Marine fabrication", "Production fabrication", "MIG welding", "TIG welding", "Stick welding", "Portable welding (MIG, TIG, stick)", "Manual lathe machining", "Knee mill machining", "Sheet metal braking (48\" capacity, 11GA mild steel)", "Ironworking (80-ton)", "Band saw cutting (13\"x21\" capacity)", "Plasma cutting", "3D modeling", "Design & engineering", "Installation", "Mirror finishing stainless steel", "In-house passivation", "Custom marine hardware", "Aluminum gangways, piers, and floats", "Cable rail system fabrication", "Custom railings", "Metal staircases", "Fireplace surrounds and screens", "Custom architectural fabrication", "Furniture metal fabrication", "Agricultural equipment fabrication and repair", "Art and museum fabrication", "Aluminum wood-fired hot tubs (Octagram Tubs)", "Shop drawing creation", "Aluminum and steel production"], "industries": ["Marine", "Residential construction", "Commercial construction", "Architecture", "Shipbuilding", "Furniture design", "Agriculture", "Museums and cultural institutions", "Art", "General contracting"], "materials": ["Steel", "Stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Bronze", "Brass"], "equipment": ["Manual lathe", "Knee mill", "48\" sheet metal brake (11GA mild steel capacity)", "80-ton ironworker", "13\"x21\" band saw", "Plasma cutter", "Portable MIG/TIG/stick welders", "MIG welders", "TIG welders", "Stick welders"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Design, engineer, build, finish, and install in-house", "Over 8,000 lineal feet