UPDATE companies SET description='Momentive Technologies is headquartered in Strongsville, Ohio. The company traces its roots back more than 130 years, though a specific founding year is not disclosed.

The company manufactures fused quartz, ceramic components, crucibles, heaters, and high‑thermal‑conductivity graphite. Its processes include customizing quartz by dimension, purity, bubble content, and coating, as well as applying ceramic coatings. Momentive operates 10 facilities across Asia, Europe, and North America, employs over 900 people worldwide, and sells into 30 countries.

Its materials serve the silicon semiconductor, compound semiconductor, electronics, aerospace, lighting, and telecommunications industries. Customers include scientists, developers, and manufacturers who require high‑purity quartz for wafer processing, durable ceramics for high‑temperature environments, and graphite for thermal management in electric vehicles and AI hardware.

Momentive differentiates itself as the self‑described global leader in fused quartz, citing exclusive access to one of the purest quartz mines in the United States. The company emphasizes unmatched purity, consistency, and stability, along with a set of guiding principles — determination, precision, responsiveness, trustworthiness, integrity, and intelligent risk‑taking — that shape its approach to custom, scalable solutions.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Fused quartz manufacturing", "Ceramic component manufacturing", "Crucible production", "Heater manufacturing", "High thermal conductivity graphite production", "Custom quartz fabrication (dimension, purity, bubble content, coating)", "Ceramic coating application"], "industries": ["Silicon Semiconductor", "Compound Semiconductor", "Electronics", "Aerospace", "Lighting", "Telecommunications"], "materials": ["Fused quartz", "Ceramics", "Graphite", "High thermal conductivity graphite"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Self\u2011described global leader in fused quartz", "Exclusive access to one of the purest U.S. quartz mines", "Customizable quartz by dimension, purity, bubble content, and coating", "10 manufacturing facilities across three continents", "Over 130 years of materials expertise"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Strongsville, Ohio -> /", "Over 130 years of history -> /about-us", "900+ employees worldwide -> /about-us", "10 facilities in Asia, Europe, North America -> /about-us", "Sells in 30 countries -> /about-us", "Products: fused quartz, ceramics, crucibles, heaters, high thermal conductivity graphite -> /", "Industries: Silicon Semiconductor, Compound Semiconductor, Electronics, Aerospace -> /about-us", "Also serves lighting, telecommunications -> /", "Customizable by dimension, purity, bubble content, coating -> db", "Ceramic coatings -> db", "Global leader in fused quartz claim -> /", "Original user to one of the purest quartz mines in the U.S. -> /", "ISO certifications mentioned (no specifics) -> /about-us", "Guiding principles listed -> /about-us", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "our advanced quartz, ceramics, crucibles and heaters are at the core of technology and progress", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "900+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/momentivetech/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='momentive-technologies' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Monarch Plastics Inc, operating as The Monarch Group, is headquartered in Kenosha, Wisconsin. Founded more than 50 years ago, the company has built a reputation as a specialist in plastic packaging solutions for growing brands and the partners that serve them.

The company designs, tools, and produces custom HDPE containers, PET cans, and a range of stock containers. Its in‑house capabilities include manufacturing, container decoration, and automated palletizing, all supported by vertical integration that allows tooling, development, and production under one roof.

Monarch serves food manufacturers, retail chains, and consumer‑packaged‑goods brands. A vice president of a Canadian food manufacturer noted that Monarch’s custom HDPE containers meet the stringent packaging requirements of Canada’s largest retailers, illustrating the company’s reach into North American retail supply chains.

