UPDATE companies SET description='Morgen Woodwork operates from Purchase, New York, where founder Gary began woodworking as a hobby in 1992 in the basement of his home. Inspired by television woodworkers and authors, he spent the next 28 years refining his craft and producing hundreds of pieces before turning the pursuit into a full-time vocation.

The shop creates bespoke furniture for every room in the home, including dining and living rooms, bedrooms, offices, bathrooms, and outdoor spaces. Each project starts with a collaborative design process, often initiated through a virtual consultation, and progresses through handcrafted construction in Gary''s workshop. Output is measured in individual commissions rather than volume runs, with hundreds of unique pieces completed over nearly three decades.

Clients are primarily residential customers seeking tailored solutions for specific spaces and aesthetics. A testimonial from Melissa Shapiro-Bey, Director of Ecommerce Operations at West Elm, highlights a custom desk built for a New York City apartment, illustrating the shop''s ability to meet exacting dimensional and stylistic requirements. The portfolio also includes categories such as spiritual items, music-related pieces, and decorative objects.

Gary emphasizes that the distinguishing feature of Morgen Woodwork is the co-creative experience: clients participate in the design, resulting in heirloom-quality pieces that reflect both function and personal narrative. The company does not mass-produce; instead, it aims to deliver furniture that customers value for the role they played in its creation.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom woodworking", "Furniture design", "Client collaboration", "Virtual consultation", "Bespoke furniture fabrication"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Walnut"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["No mass production; every piece is one-of-a-kind", "Collaborative design process with client involvement", "Heirloom-quality craftsmanship", "Virtual consultation available for remote clients", "Over 28 years of woodworking experience"], "facts_used": ["Location: Purchase, NY -> db", "Founder Gary started hobby in 1992 -> /about", "Business evolved from hobby to full-time vocation -> /about", "Custom woodworking, collaborative design, virtual consultation -> /, /about", "Hundreds of pieces over 28 years -> /about", "Product categories: decor, dining/living room, bedroom, office, bathroom, outdoor, spiritual, music -> /", "Testimonial from Melissa Shapiro-Bey, West Elm -> /", "Product example: Cabinet in Walnut -> db", "No mass production, heirloom-quality focus -> /about", "Co-creative experience as differentiator -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "I don''t mass produce my pieces. We collaborate to design a piece that not only provides the needed function, but complements its surroundings in aesthetic, space, and architectural style.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='morgen-woodwork' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Morningstar Auto Parts operates an auto parts store in Staten Island, New York. The business serves the surrounding communities including New Dorp, Great Kills, Eltingville, and several northern New Jersey towns such as Carteret, Linden, and Elizabeth. No founding year or ownership details are publicly disclosed.

The company stocks a range of original equipment and aftermarket components for popular cars and trucks, covering fuel and exhaust systems, radiators and cooling, suspension, and transmission parts. In addition to parts sales, Morningstar provides custom paint services, paint supplies, machine shop work including welding, and hazardous waste removal through partner vendors. The shop also offers counter service, heavy-duty vehicle support, and express courier delivery.

The company highlights its ability to locate hard-to-find parts and cites a customer testimonial describing same-day delivery of a part sourced within minutes and priced significantly below dealership quotes.

