UPDATE companies SET description='North Dakota Telephone Company (NDTC) began operation in 1993 as a multi-faceted telecommunications provider headquartered in Devils Lake, North Dakota. The company is owned by a consortium of three area telephone cooperatives—United Telephone Mutual Aid Cooperative of Langdon, Dakota Central Rural Telephone Cooperative of Carrington, and Polar Communications of Park River—giving it a locally rooted ownership structure.

NDTC delivers a suite of communications services including unlimited local and long-distance telephone, high-speed internet access, digital television, computer networking and wiring, website hosting, surveillance equipment, and dedicated data circuits. The company serves more than 11,000 customers across northeastern North Dakota with a staff of over 60 local employees who live and work in the communities they serve.

Its customer base spans residential subscribers, businesses, and community institutions throughout the region, including towns such as Cando, Fessenden, Harvey, Leeds, McVille, New Rockford, and Tolna. NDTC is also a member-owner of North Dakota Long Distance (NDLD) and Dakota Carrier Network (DCN), which provide statewide long-distance and carrier-grade Ethernet, wavelength, and Wi-Fi services. In 2003, NDTC helped establish North Plains Utility Contracting to handle underground construction for its network and other utilities.

The company emphasizes community reinvestment as a differentiator. Since 1995, its Dollars in Motion program has granted over $1 million to local schools, non-profits, and community projects, and it awards ten $1,000 scholarships annually to graduating seniors. Employees volunteer regularly, sponsor local events, and partner with food banks and sports leagues. NDTC’s stated mission is to provide a quality communication network that strengthens communities, guided by core values of reliability, service, accountability, integrity, growth, and communication.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Unlimited local telephone service", "Long distance telephone service", "High speed internet access", "Digital TV", "Computer networking, wiring, & maintenance", "Web site hosting", "Surveillance equipment", "Dedicated data circuits", "Managed Wi-Fi", "CommandIQ app", "Fiber internet"], "industries": ["Telecommunications", "Broadband Internet", "Cable Television", "Computer Networking", "Web Hosting", "Security Surveillance", "Data Communications", "Utility Construction"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["CommandIQ app", "Managed Wi-Fi equipment", "Fiber optic network"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Locally owned by three telephone cooperatives, ensuring decisions benefit the community", "Over 60 employees reside in the service area, providing personalized support", "Dollars in Motion program has invested over $1 million in local projects since 1995", "Member-owner of statewide networks NDLD and DCN for enhanced reliability", "Awards ten $1,000 scholarships each year to area graduating seniors"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1993 -> /about-us", "Headquarters Devils Lake, ND -> /about-us", "Owned by consortium of three cooperatives -> /about-us", "Over 11,000 customers -> /about-us", "Over 60 employees -> /about-us", "Services list (telephone, internet, TV, networking, hosting, surveillance, data circuits) -> /about-us", "Member-owner of NDLD (est. 1996) -> /about-us", "Member-owner of DCN (est. 1996) -> /about-us", "Helped establish NPUC in 2003 -> /about-us", "Member of BAND -> /about-us", "Community volunteer work and sponsorships -> /about-us", "10 annual $1,000 scholarships -> /about-us", "Dollars in Motion program since 1995, over $1M granted -> /about-us", "Mission, vision, core values -> /about-us", "Website gondtc.com -> db", "Social media icons (Twitter, Facebook, Pinterest, Instagram) -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "North Dakota Telephone Company (NDTC) began operation in 1993 as a multi-faceted telecommunications company headquartered in Devils Lake, North Dakota.", "founded_year": "1993", "employee_count": "over 60", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ndtc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='NEOTech is headquartered in Longmont, Colorado. While its founding year is not publicly disclosed, NEOTech has grown through acquisitions, including the purchase of Virtex, to become a multi-site electronics manufacturing services provider.

The company specializes in advanced printed circuit board assembly (PCBA) for low-to-medium volume, high-mix programs that demand high reliability. Its core services span electronic manufacturing services, microelectronics assembly, engineering design, box and system build, and design-for-test and design-for-fabrication support. NEOTech emphasizes supply chain management and operates strategically located facilities to deliver end-to-end manufacturing from concept to customer.

NEOTech serves aerospace and defense, medical equipment, high-tech industrial, digital media, energy, and telecommunications markets. Its customer base includes prime defense contractors such as Northrop Grumman, aviation OEMs, and manufacturers of digital projector products using TI DLP technology. The firm also supports connected device development for the Internet of Things sector.

