UPDATE companies SET description='NHanced Semiconductors, Inc. operates from three U.S. locations: Batavia, Illinois; Morrisville, North Carolina; and Odon, Indiana. The company is U.S.-based and U.S.-owned, and it is ITAR registered. No founding year or founders are disclosed in public materials.

The company provides end-to-end semiconductor services spanning design, back-end-of-line (BEoL) fabrication, advanced packaging, assembly, and test. Its Class 100 cleanrooms run full semiconductor processing lines for unit processes, modules, and turnkey wafer projects. Core capabilities include 2.5D and 3D integration, hybrid bonding, chiplet assembly, heterogeneous integration, additive silicon manufacturing, photonics, microfluidics, and III‑V compound semiconductors. The Foundry 2.0 model emphasizes flexible manufacturing lines that accommodate prototype through full‑production volumes, with a focus on high‑mix, low‑ to medium‑volume runs.

NHanced serves industrial, medical, military, and scientific markets. Customers bring designs for specialized sensors, FPGAs, SerDes, memory chips (DRAM, MRAM, RRAM), ASICs, and AI systems. The firm tailors each process step for custom silicon sensors and welcomes experimental devices and small lots.

NHanced states it has delivered more distinct hybrid‑bonded projects than any other provider worldwide. Its team averages over 20 years of experience, and the company earned the 2024 3D InCites Award for Best Place to Work in Microelectronics. The business was built to address smaller market segments that need cost‑effective, high‑mix manufacturing at low and medium volumes.', certifications=ARRAY['ITAR registered']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Semiconductor design services (analog/digital physical design, mixed-signal verification, characterization, qualification)", "BEoL processing (unit processes, modules, turnkey wafer projects)", "Advanced packaging: hybrid bonding for 3D/2.5D devices", "Chiplet assembly and heterogeneous integration", "Additive silicon manufacturing", "Photonics integration", "Microfluidics integration", "III-V compound semiconductor processing", "Advanced package assembly", "Custom silicon sensor development", "Testing: thermal cycling, HAST, probe testing", "Supply chain management / Foundry 2.0 model", "High-mix, low- to medium-volume manufacturing"], "industries": ["Industrial", "Medical", "Military", "Scientific"], "materials": ["III-V compound semiconductors", "Silicon", "Heterogeneous materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to full production, low to medium volumes", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Delivered more distinct hybrid\u2011bonded projects than any other provider worldwide", "U.S.-based, U.S.-owned, and ITAR registered", "Welcomes low\u2011 and mid\u2011volume runs of complex devices alongside full production", "Class 100 cleanrooms with full semiconductor processing equipment lines", "Staff experience averaging over 20 years"], "facts_used": ["Locations (Batavia IL, Morrisville NC, Odon IN) -> /about-us", "US-based, US-owned, ITAR registered -> /about-us", "End-to-end semiconductor services (design, BEoL, packaging, assembly, test) -> /services", "Class 100 cleanrooms, full semiconductor processing equipment lines -> /services", "Capabilities: 2.5D/3D integration, hybrid bonding, chiplet assembly, heterogeneous integration, additive silicon manufacturing, photonics, microfluidics, III-V compound semiconductors -> /services", "Foundry 2.0 model, flexible manufacturing lines, prototype to full production, high-mix low/medium volume -> /services, /", "Industries served: industrial, medical, military, scientific -> /, /services", "Customer examples: sensors, FPGAs, SerDes, memory chips (DRAM, MRAM, RRAM), ASICs, AI systems -> /about-us", "Custom silicon sensors specialty -> /services", "Delivered more distinct hybrid-bonded projects than anyone else -> /about-us", "Staff experience averaging over 20 years -> /about-us", "2024 3D InCites Award for Best Place to Work in Microelectronics -> /about-us", "Focus on smaller market segments, cost-effective high-mix manufacturing at low/medium volumes -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db", "Headquarters city/state -> db", "Company name -> db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are an independent provider of semiconductor services.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/nhancedsemi/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='nhanced-semiconductors-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='It is funded through a cooperative agreement with the National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST) in the U.S. Department of Commerce, with additional support from its member organizations.

The institute runs a structured solicitation process — Requests for Proposals, Information, and Applications — to fund technical projects in areas such as intelligent biomanufacturing, advanced process analytics, process intensification, and next‑generation biotherapeutic platforms. It also administers workforce initiatives including the NIIMBL eXperience for Educators and a Faculty Fellows sabbatical program.

Its membership spans large and small biopharmaceutical companies, academic institutions, non‑profits, and government agencies. As of June 2023, industry partners represented 51 % of members, academia 30 %, non‑profits 16 %, and government 3 %. Member companies cited in testimonials include GlaxoSmithKline, AstraZeneca, and Bristol Myers Squibb. The institute serves the broader biopharmaceutical manufacturing ecosystem, including medical countermeasure development and biodefense.

NIIMBL’s stated differentiators center on its public–private model that enables pre‑competitive collaboration, accelerates the translation of innovative manufacturing technologies, and strengthens domestic supply‑chain resilience. The organization aims to enhance U.S. economic security, increase global competitiveness, and bring life‑saving medicines to market faster.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Collaborative biopharmaceutical manufacturing platform development", "Technology de-risking and adoption support", "Workforce training program administration (NIIMBL eXperience, Faculty Fellows)", "Project funding via RFP, RFI, RFA solicitations", "Advanced process analytics and real-time manufacturing control research", "Intelligent biomanufacturing through AI and digitalization", "Process intensification and advanced manufacturing platforms", "Platform technologies for emerging and next-generation biotherapeutics", "Cross-regional workforce development solutions", "Digitally fluent biomanufacturing workforce development"], "industries": ["Biopharmaceutical manufacturing", "Biotechnology", "Pharmaceutical industry", "Medical countermeasures", "Biodefense", "Workforce development and education"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Public\u2013private partnership funded by NIST/Department of Commerce", "Member-driven project funding through RFP/RFI/RFA process", "Focus on pre\u2011competitive collaboration across industry, academia, and government", "Workforce development programs for K\u201112 educators and faculty sabbaticals", "Part of the Manufacturing USA network of innovation institutes"], "facts_used": ["NIIMBL is a public-private partnership focused on advancing biopharmaceutical manufacturing -> /about", "Funded through a cooperative agreement with NIST in the U.S. Department of Commerce -> /about", "Member composition as of June 30, 2023: Industry 51%, Academia 30%, Non-p