UPDATE companies SET description='NPI Solutions was founded in May 2000 by Kevin Andersen in Morgan Hill, California, in the heart of Silicon Valley. Andersen, who had spent years in the personal computer and cable assembly boom, started the company to fill a niche for a reliable, high-throughput American manufacturer of custom electronic assemblies. The business began in a 4,000-square-foot facility and expanded globally, opening locations in Suzhou, China (2008), Singapore (2013), and Nogales, Mexico (2024). In 2022, NPI became part of the Amphenol family of companies, a global provider of interconnect, sensor, and antenna solutions.

The company specializes in complex cable assemblies, discrete wire harnesses, and full electro-mechanical box builds. Its capabilities span design engineering (mechanical, electrical, and process), prototyping, quick-turn assembly, and low-volume, high-mix production. NPI operates a Class 10,000 clean room at its Morgan Hill headquarters, supporting contamination-sensitive work for semiconductor and medical device customers. The firm also provides on-site engineering and technician services throughout Silicon Valley, with 24/7 emergency support for established clients.

NPI serves industries including semiconductor, medical device, robotics, power delivery, automotive, aerospace, IT, data communications, and military. Its customer base ranges from startups to Fortune 500 companies, with a strong concentration among Silicon Valley technology firms that require custom electro-mechanical components and secure, on-site collaboration.

NPI’s stated mission is to provide alternative manufacturing solutions that improve supply-chain efficiency and cost through flexible real-time systems, concurrent engineering, and design-for-manufacturability practices. The company emphasizes quick response times, first-rate production, experienced engineering, and data privacy—particularly for semiconductor clients—as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 13485:2016','UL 817','UL 508A']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cable assembly manufacturing", "Wire harness manufacturing", "Electro-mechanical assembly", "Box build assembly", "Design engineering (mechanical, electrical, process)", "Prototyping", "Quick-turn assembly", "Low-volume high-mix manufacturing", "On-site engineering services", "On-site technician services", "Clean room assembly (Class 10,000)", "Incoming and inline inspection", "Corrective action program", "Coaxial, Twinax, and Triax cable assembly", "Multi-conductor jacketed cable assembly", "Power cable assembly", "Flat cable assembly", "3D modeling and prototyping", "Concurrent engineering", "Design for manufacturability"], "industries": ["Semiconductor", "Medical device", "Robotics", "Power delivery", "Automotive", "Aerospace", "IT", "Data communications", "Military", "Commercial"], "materials": ["Coaxial cable", "Twinax cable", "Triax cable", "Multi-conductor jacketed cable", "Flat cable"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["On-site engineering and technician services in Silicon Valley with 24/7 emergency support", "Class 10,000 clean room for medical and semiconductor assemblies", "ISO 13485:2016 and ISO 9001 certified quality management", "UL 817 and UL 508A certified for wiring harnesses and industrial control panels", "Global manufacturing footprint across four sites (California, China, Singapore, Mexico)"], "facts_used": ["Founded May 2000 by Kevin Andersen in Morgan Hill, CA -> /about", "Started in 4,000 sq ft facility -> /about", "Global expansion: Suzhou 2008, Singapore 2013, Nogales 2024 -> /about", "Acquired by Amphenol in 2022 -> /about", "ISO 13485:2016 certified by DQS Inc. -> /quality", "ISO 9001 certified -> /quality", "UL 817 (Wiring Harness) and UL 508A (Industrial Control Panels) certified -> /about", "Class 10,000 clean room at Morgan Hill -> /about", "On-site engineering services in Silicon Valley, 24/7 emergency support -> /", "Industries served: semiconductor, medical device, robotics, power delivery, automotive, aerospace, IT, data communications, military -> /about, /", "Capabilities: cable assembly, wire harness, electro-mechanical assembly, box build, design engineering, prototyping, quick-turn, low-volume high-mix -> /about, /", "Mission: alternative manufacturing solutions to improve efficiency and costs -> /about, /quality", "Team: Keith Andersen (General Manager), Bishop McElvaney (Director of Operations) -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "NPI Solutions is a leading provider of contract design, custom OEM manufacturing, and technical services for complex electrical-mechanical assemblies, cables and harnesses", "founded_year": "2000", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='npi-solutions' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
