UPDATE companies SET description='NRI Electronics Inc. operates from Anoka, Minnesota, where it has served clients for over 40 years. The company was acquired by Electrical Components International (ECI) in 2019, becoming part of a larger engineered-components organization.

As an electronics manufacturing services (EMS) provider, NRI specializes in printed circuit board assembly, custom wire and cable harness assembly, and electro‑mechanical manufacturing. Its Anoka facility runs surface‑mount lines equipped with automated stencil printers, high‑speed pick‑and‑place machines, automated optical inspection, and multi‑zone reflow ovens. Additional capabilities include conformal coating and potting, X‑ray and circuit‑assembly debugging, wire cutting and marking, braiding up to three inches in diameter, splicing, and full inspection and test services. The shop handles prototype, pilot, and low‑to‑high‑volume runs.

The company’s customer base spans aerospace, law enforcement, and military sectors. NRI builds aerospace mechanical and electronic assemblies, produces electronics for military and law‑enforcement applications, and works with automotive wire types such as GXL, SXL, and TXL.

NRI emphasizes a quality culture built on the core values of integrity, commitment, and teamwork. It cites 100 % on‑time delivery, Six Sigma quality metrics, and a “sophisticated planning and production management” system as differentiators. Customers note the firm’s personal service, rapid response to field issues, and willingness to provide design‑phase input.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB Assembly (SMT)", "Custom Wire Harness Assembly", "Custom Cable Assembly", "Electro-Mechanical Assembly", "Conformal Coating", "Potting", "Diagnostic Services (X-Ray & Circuit Assembly Debugging)", "Wire Cutting and Marking", "Braiding (1/8\"-3\" diameter)", "Splicing", "Automated Optical Inspection (AOI)", "Circuit Testing", "Engineering Design Services", "Sophisticated Planning & Production Management", "Mating Harness Test Fixtures", "Plotted Layout Assembly Guide (prototypes, pilot, low-volume)"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Law Enforcement", "Military"], "materials": ["Automotive wire types (GXL, SXL, TXL)"], "equipment": ["Automated stencil printers", "High-speed pick-and-place machines", "Automated optical inspection (AOI) systems", "Multi-zone reflow ovens", "X-Ray inspection equipment"], "volume": "Low to high volume; prototypes, pilot, and low-volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% on-time delivery and Six Sigma quality metrics", "Sophisticated planning and production management system", "Personal service with rapid response to field issues", "Quality culture rooted in integrity, commitment, and teamwork", "Design-phase collaboration and flexibility for changes"], "facts_used": ["Location: Anoka, Minnesota -> db", "Acquired by Electrical Components International (ECI) in 2019 -> /", "Over 40 years of service -> /", "EMS supplier specializing in PCB Assembly, Custom Harness Assembly and Electro Mechanical Manufacturing -> /", "SMT lines with automated stencil printers, high-speed pick & place, AOI, m