UPDATE companies SET description='Nelson Steel Products Inc operates from Holland, Michigan. By 1959 the business incorporated as Nelson Steel Products, Inc., and a 1968 U.S. Army trailer-frame contract spurred expansion into a large-scale production facility. The company remains family-led, with the founder''s sons Wally and Roger involved in its growth.

The shop provides a full range of steel fabrication services: robotic welding across 13 stations housing 17 robots, sheet and tube laser cutting, stamping and turret punching on high-volume presses, press-brake forming, tube bending, and custom prototyping.

Early work centered on agricultural implements, and the 1968 government contract established a military track record.

