UPDATE companies SET description='Netech Corporation, headquartered in Farmingdale, New York, has been designing and manufacturing biomedical test equipment since 1987. The company operates as an SBA 8(a)‑certified small business and holds a GSA contract (V797P‑4228B) with the Veterans Administration. All instruments are produced in the United States.

The product line spans defibrillator analyzers, electrical safety analyzers, pressure meters, patient simulators (including ECG, EEG, and SpO₂ waveform generation), gas flow analyzers, infusion pump analyzers, and dedicated pacemaker analyzers such as the EXPMT 2000. Netech’s engineering team develops new models in‑house — recent additions include the MiniSim EEG 2000 multi‑channel EEG simulator — and every unit ships with a NIST‑traceable calibration certificate backed by a two‑year warranty.

The company’s defibrillator and pacemaker analyzers carry FDA 510(k) clearance, and all devices are FDA listed and CE marked for international distribution.

